IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`
IMPORT `je54-art01-commencement`

-- je54-art01-by-date: Article 1 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 asked with dates.  It composes the vintage table (the text of the Law in force on a day) with the paragraph-by-paragraph rules of je54-art01-commencement.
--
-- Fork I1 (NOTES.md section 6): which day selects the text of the Law that is read for the commencement of an enactment.  Three readings, each callable; the default is the first.
--   (a) TAKEN (the brief's default): for an enactment made before 28 September 2021, compute its commencement under the text of Articles 1(5) and 1(6) in force on the day it was made, which gives a candidate day.
--       If the candidate day is before 28 September 2021 the text governs and the answer carries the basis of that text.  If it is on or after 28 September 2021, those Articles no longer exist (deleted that day,
--       L.8/2021) and the commencement is governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, which this row does not encode: the answer is the candidate day with the basis "governed by the 2021 Law, Article 3(2)".
--       For an enactment made on or after 28 September 2021 the function refuses, naming that Law.  Not circular: the candidate is computed first and then compared with 28 September 2021.
--   (b) the text in force on the day the enactment was made.
--   (c) the text in force on the day the question is asked (the enum constructor is `the day on which the question about the enactment is asked`).
-- On (a) and (b) the day is the same in every case and only the governing provision (the basis) differs; on (c) an enactment asked about from 28 September 2021 refuses.
-- That the 2021 Law gives the same day for a named day (the start of that day) was the brief's claim and is now checked.  Checked by the integrator on 2026-10-28: Article 3(2) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 reads "it is treated as coming into force at the beginning of that day, unless provision is made to the contrary" (subject je/legislation-2021, source/l_8_2021.current.txt, line 48); it does not say whether a stated time of day is such a provision (fork L2 of that row).
--
-- "Comes into operation" (Article 1(4)) and "comes into force" (the 2021 Law, the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014) are treated as the same event (assumed, not ruled); the names say "comes into force".
-- Selecting dates for the other paragraphs: Article 1(7), the day the enactment was passed or made; Articles 1(1), 1(2) and 1(3), the day the question is asked about.

§ `Article 1 asked with dates`

-- src:187 | Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:188 | L.8/2021
-- src:189 | 28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
-- src:190 | P.26/2021
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, row L.8/2021 (src:187-190)
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day on which Articles 1(5) and 1(6) are no longer in the text` MEANS YMD 2021 9 28

-- No provision: this refuses for an input that the reading chosen needs and the caller did not give.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1: the day the question is asked has not been given` MEANS
    REFUSE "the reading chosen for Article 1 takes the text in force on the day the question is asked, and no such day has been given"

-- The text of the Law that is read for the commencement of an enactment, on each reading of fork I1.
-- src:187 | Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:188 | L.8/2021
-- src:189 | 28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
-- src:190 | P.26/2021
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, row L.8/2021 (src:187-190)
GIVEN reading IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement` TYPICALLY `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`
      c IS A `Commencement as stated`
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`Article 1: the text of the Law read for the commencement of the enactment` reading c MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
    WHEN `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021` THEN `the text of the Law in force on` (c's `the day it was passed or made`)
    WHEN `the day the enactment was passed or made` THEN `the text of the Law in force on` (c's `the day it was passed or made`)
    WHEN `the day on which the question about the enactment is asked` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the day the question is asked`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `Article 1: the day the question is asked has not been given`
        WHEN JUST asked THEN `the text of the Law in force on` asked

-- The day on which the enactment comes into force.
-- src:187 | Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:188 | L.8/2021
-- src:189 | 28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
-- src:190 | P.26/2021
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6), and the endnote row L.8/2021 that deleted them (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10), (src:187-190)
GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      reading IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement` TYPICALLY `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`
GIVETH A `Day with its basis`
`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` c reading MEANS
    LET r MEANS `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` (`Article 1: the text of the Law read for the commencement of the enactment` reading c) c IN
        CONSIDER reading
        WHEN `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021` THEN
            IF r's `the day` AT LEAST `the first day on which Articles 1(5) and 1(6) are no longer in the text`
            THEN `Day with its basis` WITH
                `the day` IS r's `the day`
                `the basis` IS `governed by the 2021 Law, Article 3(2)`
            ELSE r
        OTHERWISE r

-- The moment at which the enactment comes into force: the start of that day on the clock of the zone given (Article 1(5), "immediately on the expiration of the previous day").
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      zone IS A STRING
      reading IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement` TYPICALLY `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`
GIVETH A `Moment with its basis`
`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` c zone reading MEANS
    LET r MEANS `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` c reading IN
        `Moment with its basis` WITH
            `the moment` IS DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (r's `the day`) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) zone
            `the basis` IS r's `the basis`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      reading IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement` TYPICALLY `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`
GIVETH A `Yes or no with its basis`
`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force on the day` d c reading MEANS
    LET r MEANS `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` c reading IN
        `Yes or no with its basis` WITH
            `the answer` IS d AT LEAST r's `the day`
            `the basis` IS r's `the basis`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN t IS A DATETIME
      zone IS A STRING
      c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      reading IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement` TYPICALLY `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`
GIVETH A `Yes or no with its basis`
`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` t zone c reading MEANS
    LET r MEANS `Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` c zone reading IN
        `Yes or no with its basis` WITH
            `the answer` IS DATETIME_SERIAL t AT LEAST DATETIME_SERIAL (r's `the moment`)
            `the basis` IS r's `the basis`

-- Article 1(7): selecting date is the day the enactment was passed or made.
-- src:11 | (7) Where the time at which an enactment, whenever passed or made, is to come into operation is expressed or calculated by reference to its promulgation, and the date of promulgation is unknown, that date shall be deemed to be the day the enactment was passed or made.[5]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(7) (src:11)
GIVEN `the time is expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of promulgation` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the enactment was passed or made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 1(7) by date: the date of promulgation to be used` `the time is expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation` `the date of promulgation` `the day the enactment was passed or made` MEANS
    `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used`
        (`the text of the Law in force on` `the day the enactment was passed or made`)
        `the time is expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation`
        `the date of promulgation`
        `the day the enactment was passed or made`

-- Articles 1(1), 1(2) and 1(3): selecting date is the day the question is asked about.
-- src:5 | (1) In this Law and in every other enactment (as hereby defined) whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “enactment”, unless a contrary intention appears, shall mean any provision of any Law passed by the States and confirmed by Order in Council and any provision of any regulations, Order, rules, bye-laws, scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of any Order in Council or under any such Law as aforesaid.[1]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(1) (src:5)
GIVEN `the day the question is asked about` IS A DATE
      k IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1(1) on a day: the instrument is an enactment` `the day the question is asked about` k `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    `Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` (`the text of the Law in force on` `the day the question is asked about`) k `a contrary intention appears`

-- src:6 | (2) [2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), deleted by L.8/2021: placeholder in the text from 28 September 2021 (src:6)
GIVEN `the day the question is asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day it was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council` IS A DATE
      `the day it was registered by the Royal Court` IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading of Article 1(2)` TYPICALLY `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered`
      `the day the caller states` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 1(2) on a day: the day on which a Law is deemed passed` `the day the question is asked about` `the day it was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council` `the day it was registered by the Royal Court` reading `the day the caller states` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    `Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed`
        (`the text of the Law in force on` `the day the question is asked about`)
        `the day it was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council`
        `the day it was registered by the Royal Court`
        reading
        `the day the caller states`
        `a contrary intention appears`

-- src:7 | (3) In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, references to the passing or repeal of an enactment shall be construed, where appropriate, as references to the making or rescission of that enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(3) (src:7)
GIVEN `the day the question is asked about` IS A DATE
      word IS A `Word read by Article 1(3)`
      `it is appropriate to read it so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reading under Article 1(3)`
`Article 1(3) on a day: how a reference to passing or repeal is read` `the day the question is asked about` word `it is appropriate to read it so` MEANS
    `Article 1(3): how a reference to passing or repeal is read`
        (`the text of the Law in force on` `the day the question is asked about`)
        word
        `it is appropriate to read it so`
